<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan weekly forex reserves up at $1.354 bln.</title>
<headline>Pakistan weekly forex reserves up at $1.354 bln.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's foreign exchange reserves rose to $1.354 billion on November 14, from the week ago's $1.351 billion, but were lower than $1.807 billion on November 16, 1995, the State (central) Bank of Pakistan (SBP) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The central bank gave no reason for the rise.</p>
<p>The reserves included $554 million held in Pakistan and $120 million outside the country, the bank said.  </p>
<p>Following is the weekly foreign exchange reserves holdings position in Pakistan:</p>
<p>    (MLN DLRS)		NOV 14     NOV 7	Nov 16, 1995</p>
<p> TOTAL			  1,354	1,351	   1,807</p>
<p> Forex in Pakistn	     554	  574	     843</p>
<p> Forex outside Pakistan     120	   96	     253</p>
<p> Gold coins and bullion     676	  676	     707</p>
<p> Special Drawing Rights	 4	    4		 4</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
